{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20","id":1375774,"title":"Alternate Tremere Clan Flaw - NO in clan disciplines - V20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-20T02:03:15-07:00","id":1375774,"title":"Alternate Tremere Clan Flaw - NO in clan disciplines - V20","content":"This alternate clan flaw is something that I've been working on for a bit. It came to me all at once in a moment of inspiration and it comes with a fair bit of fluff that some of you may like or may wish to ignore.<br /> <br /> The jist is this. The Tremere, having been brought to the curse of Cain by unnatural means are not true vampires in the purest sense, they have no direct link to the 13 antediluvians that inherited the curses given to them by Cain but they are of Cains blood regardless, as such, these vampires are neither clanless nor are they a true clan in the traditional sense (although they have many distinctive traits that utterly separate them from the caitiff).<br /> <br /> While the Tremere possess no unique clan flaw that distinguish them from other vampire clans, they also have no unique in clan disciplines that are their own either and must learn them from other vampires who possess them, save one: thaumaturgy, the discipline of many paths.<br /> <br /> The art of magic runs in the blood of the Tremere and all who have that blood feel called to it, but unlike the other vampires who rule the night, this discipline requires study to be learned, unless the vampire is of the rarest sort. Tremere may still learn disciplines out of clan, which as per optional rules, requires them to drink the blood of another vampire, though they suffer blood bonding no worse than anyone else, and still practice the binding to the will of the clan as well as the taking of blood from every newly embraced so that it can be kept by the council of seven.<br /> <br /> keep in mind, thaumaturgy takes practice or a true calling to magic to be learned and also is blood intensive more so than any other discipline with a few exceptions for higher level powers (it always requires blood to be spent).<br /> <br /> This means that Tremere are even more likely to embrace with care, as unlike in other clans, a Tremere has no chance to learn their native disciplines intuitively (with exceptions), thus building on the insular and also very carefully built nature of the clan.<br /> <br /> lastly, as a caveat, though not a hard rule, the Tremere should be called to the path of blood first, as it is the magic over this substance that brought them, as a clan, to vampirism; it is the power which flows within their blood with the greatest primacy. The first step down the path of blood is the divinatory revelation of the true nature of vitae, and for most, it is used to divine the true nature of other vampires; but for a fledgling Tremere, it is almost always first used after a rigorous instruction in the magical arts and entails the magical discovery of the very blood that runs within them. During this first revelation, the vampire learns about their own blood and what its properties are, what vitae truly is, and what it makes them.<br /> <br /> This mystical self discovery is the first step to being able to master not only the magic of the blood, but also, the condition of vampirism itself, and also leads to a significant degree of self discovery as well. Some vampires may even learn from it, in some small subliminal way, the fashion in which the Tremere created themselves as well, and gain intuitive insights in how their clan came to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;As you came into my curse through magic, so too shall the only powers of my blood that you inherit be that magic.&quot; Thus spoke Cain in his judgement upon Tremere. Either in a moment of awakening at his blood's transmutation and the ensuing alteration to the the curse itself, or in the times of Gehenna... or perhaps both.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 10-07-2021, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:27:15-07:00","id":1375787,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a> I like your idea from a plot and mechanic perspective. Great stuff.<br /> The only drawback I can see is that it does not influence your nightly decisions. In a typical chronicle would you approach any situation different than other kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:57:16-07:00","id":1375791,"title":"","content":"The Real Reason they encourage the path of blood as the primary path is control. With something like the Lure of Flames or Movement of the Mind, it's just one thing that you can get better with. With something varied like blood, someone has to teach you each next-step, creating a dependence on teachers.<br /> <br /> I... don't mind this, OP. It's not bad. But you should also consider bloodlines. Many visilble bloodlines don't or have doubtful antideluvians or did the same thing the Tremere did. I suspect many bloodlines are created when a Caitiff eats their way up, has strong leanings towards certain disciplines, and embraces childer that have the same disposition. The blood sets a preference for disciplines and a weakness at some point along this line. If you make the Tremere Caitiff like, what do you do about Nagaraja, perhaps cacophany? (actually there aren't that many big ones, but It's implied caitiff and thin bloods manifest unique disciplines and presumably would hand them down to childer)<br /> <br /> plus... Auspex and dominate really suit the Tremere, and not all Tremere are primarily magic nerds. You've got enforcers and financial wizards to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 03-20-2020, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T06:59:59-07:00","id":1375801,"title":"","content":"From a point-value perspective, it could potentially count as one of (if not <i>THE</i>) most devastating clan flaw. In other words, if you were to reduce this to a point value so that other characters could take it at character creation, how much do you think this would be? There is no flaw &quot;One Less Clan Discipline&quot;, but the Merit &quot;Additional Clan Discipline&quot; is 5 points; accordingly, I think this would make this probably a 10+ point flaw. There's also the additional question of whether it would be intellectually honest to allow them to even start the game with the 3 basic dots of Disciplines that other vampires get at character creation. Theoretically, every newly-minted vampire just <i>has</i> those three-dots-worth of Disciplines as soon as they're embraced--but they also have in-clans disciplines.<br /> <br /> I've never understood people trying to power balance Tremere. Don't get me wrong, I understand the desire and inclination, but never understood why someone would look at the wild power disparities present across basically every single edition of old school <i>V:tM</i>, written over the course of 20+ years, and not realize that that indifference to imbalance is a <i>feature</i> of the game. In other words, this has never been a game that cared about balancing the clans or Disciplines <i>at all</i>. Potence is indisputably worlds better than its direct counterpart, Fortitude; Celerity is arguably (though I think generally accepted to be) better than both; every level of Auspex is like 3-4 powers in one; most Dominate, Presence, and Auspex powers are free; most Obfuscate powers are not only free, but <i>don't require a roll</i>. Then there are Disciplines that are unapologetically terribly--Valeren comes to mind (or, in Dark Ages lines, <i>Warrior </i>Valeren); the Level 3 and Level 5 are pretty good, but 1, 2, and 4 are hot garbage when scaled in comparison to the average 1st, 2nd, and 4th levels of Disciplines. And it's not like the Salubri Antitribu are a super esoteric clan originally found in the Storyteller's Handbook and aren't really apt to be played by PCs; on the contrary, they're right in the Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> It's not fair at all--but that's sort of the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T08:32:31-07:00","id":1375815,"title":"","content":"This is a <b><i>fantastic</i></b> idea. It's so good I can honestly say that I wish I'd thought of it, and if I were still playing Vampire in the canon WoD (where the Tremere &quot;stole&quot; their vampirism) I totally would.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing this. I'm filing this away in the back of my head to do something with it someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T08:38:37-07:00","id":1375816,"title":"","content":"Otter, you are both wrong and right. <br /> <br /> Clan specific disciplines are meant to be very powerful but very niche. All the common disciplines are broadly applicable to undead life, but being able to summon shadows? That's not a great party trick with the masquerade in mind. Obtenebration is more powerful than, say, potence because it's got way more downsides to it. But Auspex struggling against obfuscate or Potence beating out fortitude isn't really an intended feature. Thaumaturgy is in a very weird spot because of this, because it's both very broad and highly specific, and it's the only discipline that isn't strictly linear. Storytellers worry about the potential of it, rather than the reality of it. It doesn't help that Tremere players, like malkavians, are the best and worst of the table, and are more likely to powergame as the wizard. Nosferatu are also great for powergaming, but they're less of a problem because they don't really attract powergamers so much as -all the spells-. <br /> <br /> I really think it's an out-of-game problem with players. <br /> (Honestly, the fact that Tremere is so attractive to powergamers, both in that they've got the spells and the clan culture for it, is probably a canon reason why everyone hates the Tremere)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T10:44:38-07:00","id":1375833,"title":"","content":"I'm iffy on this idea, because the Tremere are intended to replicate a particular archetype of vampire: the sort of vampires who barely move and use various esoteric mystic abilities such as &quot;Love At First Bite&quot; Dracula. He hypnotizes, he uses telekinesis, he never throws a punch. Removing Dominate from their clan disciplines therefore feels off. I might make physical disciplines even more expensive than other out-of-clan Disciplines, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T13:35:57-07:00","id":1375853,"title":"","content":"So, d'you want x7 everything but Thaum or x6 for everything (maybe x5 for thaum) <br /> <br /> Lots of Tremere threads lately... <br /> <br /> While I disagree with Cajun (The Tremere are the New-Money types, whilst the Ventrue are the conservative old money elite, the Toreador are the liberal elite, and the brujah are clowns... The Tremere are meant to be agressive, domineering (dominate), prideful (thaumaturgy) and they act like they know everything (auspex) and they fall back on their status and might of their clan if things don't go their way (Yep, they're the shitty dime-a-dozen villains from chinese comics) They're graceless bulldozers in a world of charismatic vampires, using their power to compensate for their lack of charm. <br /> <br /> Now, that's a massive exaggeration, but they're very much New Money, with each edition advocating pinstriped suits and flashy jewelry (While Ventrue would advocate you tone it down a bit) <br /> In-clan disciplines are really just an expression of the type of people in the clan, and Auspex/Dominate/Thaum fit the Tremere like a glove. (Also, dominate helps smothing out getting the ingredients, Auspex helps you find the good stuff and the errors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T17:20:06-07:00","id":1375876,"title":"","content":"with regard to the comments on the Tremere's lack of auspex and dominate, I for one have allowed them to replicate disciplines with thaumaturgy, some paths do this already anyhow.<br /> <br /> with the paths of sorcery from mage the ascension, such as fascination, divination, shadow casting, you could conceivably replicate powers such as dominate, auspex and even obtenbration.<br /> <br /> now I personally don't like the idea of Tremere having access to anything that replicates obtenebration or other rare disciplines but I don't mind them having access to paths that replicate the common disciplines, and given their proclivities, I don't see why they wouldn't develop powers of sorcerous sight and mind control as well as enhanced physical ability and other powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 03-21-2020, 05:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T08:51:25-07:00","id":1375975,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a> <br /> <br /> I'll try not to be harsh, because, really the flaw is okay. It doesn't break anything. It's not difficult to administer. It doesn't disrupt the meta-plot unduly.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's umm... not harmful in any way.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> It's okay, but a little bland since pcs won't interact with the flaw on a nightly basis. I mean, in play, it consists entirely of the players looking around the table and asking, &quot;Does anyone know Auspex or Dominate?&quot;, and the Tremere playing responding with &quot;Nope. Matt, you're playing a Malk, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Think about how most flaws (Brujah, Tzimisce, Ventrue, etc.) help drive the story forward by providing positive challenges. The Brujah rages at an inappropriate moment. The Tzimisce's pack has to go on a roadtrip to get some soil. The Ventrue finds that there are fewer and fewer polka-band members lately, something must be done.<br /> <br /> As it stands in V20 canon, the Tremere flaw boils down to &quot;on occasion, the ST will use your regent to hand out quests to the players&quot;. This a moderately useful tool for STs.<br /> <br /> Your flaw exists only in the absence of a wholly optional trait most characters won't have. Playing at a game table, how would you, as ST, use a pc Tremere's clan flaw to drive the story forward or create new subplot?<br /> <br /> Since your Tremere can still learn ooc disciplines at no penalty, there will be Tremere around who know all sorts of other disciplines. Remember, that in V20&amp;pre ic and ooc disciplines cost the same for the first dot... 10 xp either way. So, your Tremere (and canon Gangrel, Nosferatu, etc.) learn Dominate 1 as easily as any Ventrue, assuming access to the blood. At dot two, the cost difference is only 4xp.<br /> <br /> So, your flaw could also be written as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clan Flaw: After many long years of focusing on magic to the exclusion of all else, the Warlocks pay the same price for the first dot of disciplines as everyone else. At higher levels, they pay slightly more than they would pay if they had the discipline in-clan, just as would any other vampire. Thaumaturgy, of course, requires a teacher, just as it does for everyone. </div> </div> </div>I am wondering, as well, what problem are you trying to fix with the canon flaw? I know it has received much scorn through the years from the fan base, but what is it that especially bothers you?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T18:35:56-07:00","id":1376048,"title":"","content":"First off, the V20 flaw IS still in place in terms of the fact that every Tremere is bound to the clan, they still have that same structure. I swear I mentioned that.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the revised edition flaw is also still in effect as well then. AS a result, the ST power to throw stuff at the player is IN effect, not out.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole you get bound to the second degree from a single drink didn't come into play much anyway to be honest. I never had a huge problem with it effecting my Tremere characters or in all my years of STing for either table top or big group LARPs to be honest. Do you feel that it came up a lot in game? the actual V20 flaw is the double blood bond thing IIRC. <br /> <br /> I like my version, it feels thematic to me and the increased XP cost for disciplines is kind of nice considering how much oomph Thaum gives players. also, it makes the tremere much more dependent on thaum in setting. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1375975#post1375975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a><br /> <br /> I'll try not to be harsh, because, really the flaw is okay. It doesn't break anything. It's not difficult to administer. It doesn't disrupt the meta-plot unduly.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it's umm... not harmful in any way.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> It's okay, but a little bland since pcs won't interact with the flaw on a nightly basis. I mean, in play, it consists entirely of the players looking around the table and asking, &quot;Does anyone know Auspex or Dominate?&quot;, and the Tremere playing responding with &quot;Nope. Matt, you're playing a Malk, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Think about how most flaws (Brujah, Tzimisce, Ventrue, etc.) help drive the story forward by providing positive challenges. The Brujah rages at an inappropriate moment. The Tzimisce's pack has to go on a roadtrip to get some soil. The Ventrue finds that there are fewer and fewer polka-band members lately, something must be done.<br /> <br /> As it stands in V20 canon, the Tremere flaw boils down to &quot;on occasion, the ST will use your regent to hand out quests to the players&quot;. This a moderately useful tool for STs.<br /> <br /> Your flaw exists only in the absence of a wholly optional trait most characters won't have. Playing at a game table, how would you, as ST, use a pc Tremere's clan flaw to drive the story forward or create new subplot?<br /> <br /> Since your Tremere can still learn ooc disciplines at no penalty, there will be Tremere around who know all sorts of other disciplines. Remember, that in V20&amp;pre ic and ooc disciplines cost the same for the first dot... 10 xp either way. So, your Tremere (and canon Gangrel, Nosferatu, etc.) learn Dominate 1 as easily as any Ventrue, assuming access to the blood. At dot two, the cost difference is only 4xp.<br /> <br /> So, your flaw could also be written as:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am wondering, as well, what problem are you trying to fix with the canon flaw? I know it has received much scorn through the years from the fan base, but what is it that especially bothers you?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T02:06:09-07:00","id":1376082,"title":"","content":"it realIy doesn't give that much umph, not less we're talking DT or maybe Mercury or we're talking about rituals (as I've said, give other players backgrounds) <br /> <br /> <br /> So, with that considered, what are you going to do about sorcerer assamites who also have in-clan magic. What about necromancers? Settites and Tzmisce both have access to OoC blood magic, whilst <i>Rites of the Blood </i>was really nice to anarch sorcerers. <br /> <br /> It's not that the Tremere are strong, it's that they attract powergamers, which makes Tremere seem strong. All the clans work for a powergamer, Tremere just have more obvious appeal. The Tremere flaw was always that nobody else liked them. The more I read your posts, the more it seems you just dislike them. (That in-universe stuff is way to effective!) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T16:10:04-07:00","id":1376167,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a> <br /> <br /> Oh, okay. I'm sorry I didn't realize that you meant they still had the clan flaw from V20, p69.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weaknesses: Tremere dependency on blood is even<br /> more pronounced than that of other Kindred. It takes<br /> only two draughts of another vampire\u2019s blood for a<br /> Tremere to become blood bound instead of the normal<br /> three \u2014 the first drink counts as if the Tremere had taken<br /> two drinks. (For more information on the blood bond, see<br /> p. 286). The elders of the Clan are well aware of this, and<br /> seek to impart loyalty to the Clan by forcing all neonate<br /> Warlocks to drink of the (transubstantiated) blood of the<br /> seven Tremere elders soon after their Embrace. </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure why I took the following to mean that they &quot;possess no unique clan flaw&quot;... such as becoming bound after two drinks rather than three.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the Tremere possess no unique clan flaw that distinguish them from other vampire clans... </div> </div> </div>It was my mistake. I should have read more carefully. I may have been confused by this part of your post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..., though they suffer blood bonding no worse than anyone else,... </div> </div> </div>Since your post was titled &quot;Alternate Clan Flaw&quot; I also thought you meant the loss of Auspex and Dominate was <i>instead</i> of the V20 flaw, rather than in addition to it.<br /> <br /> Again, sorry for misreading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T17:55:08-07:00","id":1376188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1376082#post1376082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it realIy doesn't give that much umph, not less we're talking DT or maybe Mercury or we're talking about rituals (as I've said, give other players backgrounds)<br /> <br /> <br /> So, with that considered, what are you going to do about sorcerer assamites who also have in-clan magic. What about necromancers? Settites and Tzmisce both have access to OoC blood magic, whilst <i>Rites of the Blood </i>was really nice to anarch sorcerers.<br /> <br /> It's not that the Tremere are strong, it's that they attract powergamers, which makes Tremere seem strong. All the clans work for a powergamer, Tremere just have more obvious appeal. The Tremere flaw was always that nobody else liked them. The more I read your posts, the more it seems you just dislike them. (That in-universe stuff is way to effective!)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're wrong, I love the Tremere, they're my favourite clan.<br /> <br /> secondly, im not advocating anyone else change their game, I just like this version of the flaw, I think its fucking cool.<br /> <br /> as for the other sorcerers, let them be. I never said to change them. secondly, the tremere have way more paths than the koldun snd assamites in V20. the list of powers for those 2 clans is lower for them. what do the Koldun have, 4?<br /> <br /> not sure about the Setite paths. <br /> <br /> Also, with regard to those 3 clans, I personally (and this is just me) have depicted their magic as heavily religious based with a smaller number of in clan paths and also, a traditional style that is not given to innovation in the same way the Tremere's thaumaturgy is.<br /> <br /> but hey, I get the flaw is just not for you, but please don't get the wrong impression and misunderstand this flaw idea that I put out there for others to use, im a dyed in the wool tremere fan not an opponent to the clan. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 03-22-2020, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T18:00:42-07:00","id":1376189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1376167#post1376167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a><br /> <br /> Oh, okay. I'm sorry I didn't realize that you meant they still had the clan flaw from V20, p69.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure why I took the following to mean that they &quot;possess no unique clan flaw&quot;... such as becoming bound after two drinks rather than three.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was my mistake. I should have read more carefully. I may have been confused by this part of your post:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since your post was titled &quot;Alternate Clan Flaw&quot; I also thought you meant the loss of Auspex and Dominate was <i>instead</i> of the V20 flaw, rather than in addition to it.<br /> <br /> Again, sorry for misreading.</div> </div> </div> </div>no, you actually got it. I don't like the double blood bonding thing as I think its not as effective in game to game situations and doesn't add much to the theme of the game. I like the revised era flaw that every tremere is blood bound to the clan itself and also has their blood given to the local regent and the council of seven for various disciplinary purposes. <br /> <br /> I also like adding this to the mix. I genuinely feel its thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T18:04:27-07:00","id":1376190,"title":"","content":"Vampire Translation Guide had the great idea of making the Tremere a Covenant becuase they actually work like one...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T18:11:25-07:00","id":1376192,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As a flaw this is genuinely not going to be much more effective in night to night games at enforcing a unique theme than the existing flaw in V 20, in which all that happens is you get blood bonded easier.<br /> <br /> The V20 flaw has never been deemed especially pressing for the Tremere, nor did it you give the same sort of role playing opportunities that the other clan flaws provided and to be honest I don't think this flaw is either. However, I feel it has more thematic impact then the double blood bonding floor of V 20</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T03:30:21-07:00","id":1376235,"title":"","content":"The V20 Tremere flaw is more pressing when you're in an anarch game. I've never played with sabbat Tremere so I don't know much about that. In a camarilla game, the implication is still there; You are bound to the clan. A magical flaw works metaphysically better than purely social one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T15:18:54-07:00","id":1376317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1375816#post1375816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Auspex struggling against obfuscate or Potence beating out fortitude isn't really an intended feature.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree strongly with this sentence; moreso with the second part than the first. I don't know that Auspex &quot;struggles&quot; against Obfuscate, inasmuch as they seem perfectly balanced. If your Auspex is higher than someone's Obfuscate, you see through it automatically; if their Obfuscate is higher, you're fooled automatically. If they're even, you roll off, and only in the event of a tie does the defender (i.e., the obfuscate user) take the square. That's pretty even; the only way it could be more even would be if, instead of ties going to the defender, the players just had to keep rolling off until one person won--that would be a <i>de minimis</i> change; more for edge cases than anything else.<br /> <br /> I very strongly disagree your statement about Potence v. Fortitude though--i.e., that Potence beating out Fortitude isn't an intended feature. How could it be the case that someone designed the game with two powers that work <i>directly </i>against one another (one assisting damage rolls, and the other assisting soak rolls), but it not be an intentional shift in the power dynamics and tone of the game to make it so that the power that assists damage rolls is vastly and incomparably better than the power that assists soak rolls? Do you really believe that it was never brought to the designers' attention that an attacker with as much Potence as the defender has Fortitude, is incredibly favored? I will submit to you that even if when they wrote it all out that <i>wasn't </i>the intention, the moment it was pointed out to them, and they did nothing about it, they ratified the power imbalance as not-a-problem-here and it became their intent to make a game in which causing damage was incredibly easier than absorbing or preventing damage.<br /> <br /> Not only that, the fact alone that Celerity changed so much from one edition to the next (between how much blood you needed to spend for extra actions, all the way to V20 where your celerity buffs your Dex rolls when you're actively using them for extra turns), but that Potence has always been automatic successes, and Fortitude has always been dice, only further drives home the fact that despite the fact that they were willing to adjust how physical disciplines worked between editions--the fact that it's easier to cause damage than take it was always, at a minimum, perfectly acceptable. To their credit, they absolutely made a world that is Very Dark and Dangerous<b>\u2122.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:27:55-07:00","id":1384252,"title":"","content":"how many paths of thaum are there?<br /> <br /> does anyone have a accurate count?<br /> <br /> it influences the severity of this flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T16:22:47-07:00","id":1384295,"title":"","content":"I mean, what's wrong with the Tremere? Why you guys hate them so much?<br /> I think this kind of post is a shame, since your only trying to add difficult for the players, relying on a huge nerf, it's not cool if you pair the house clan/house with caitiff, that's what you trying to do.<br /> It doesn't matter if the tremere have access to more paths and rituals, it's how your pcs will use them in the game that will make them great or losers.<br /> Kolduns are waaaaaaaaaayyyy more powerful than any other school, in a way that you can't even understand how.<br /> You don't like this clan mate, you actually hate then, just take a look at how a PC can get new paths or rituals, being blood bonded to everyone in the chantry or who has a higher mistery circle than him. It's incredible difficult to get powerful paths and play properly with them, it takes time.<br /> And now you come with a huge idea...&quot;Why don't we give a 10 points flaw to the clan or whoever tries to play tremere because I hate them&quot;.<br /> It would've been nicer of your part to say in the begging of the post &quot;I got facerolled by a tremere with my Ventrue and lost my dignitas&quot; before all this text.<br /> <br /> Great idea! Let's make the clan Tremere Caitiff's! Jeezz<br /> <br /> Dur-An-Ki has paths that makes your life miserable and they don't even need to leave their havens.<br /> Koldun paths are so powerful that one of them can make a freaking volcano out of nowhere and the player can cast this 5 kms away from you...and all kraina are incredible strong, Jesus dude, you can talk with demons and you don't even need a high level requirement for that, you can &quot;farm&quot; Will Power like water. It's totally inconceivable for me to understand this kind of nerf that you want with the tremere. It's a shame mate, it's a real shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","user":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","date":". 04-27-2020, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"r