/> <br /> Great idea! Let's make the clan Tremere Caitiff's! Jeezz<br /> <br /> Dur-An-Ki has paths that makes your life miserable and they don't even need to leave their havens.<br /> Koldun paths are so powerful that one of them can make a freaking volcano out of nowhere and the player can cast this 5 kms away from you...and all kraina are incredible strong, Jesus dude, you can talk with demons and you don't even need a high level requirement for that, you can &quot;farm&quot; Will Power like water. It's totally inconceivable for me to understand this kind of nerf that you want with the tremere. It's a shame mate, it's a real shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>did you even read the fucking thread?<br /> <br /> I LOVE THE TREMERE. <br /> <br /> that's why I made the flaw. so they'd be more unique. <br /> <br /> its not like I hate them, and I said that earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T00:46:21-07:00","id":1384377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1376317#post1376317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree strongly with this sentence; moreso with the second part than the first. I don't know that Auspex &quot;struggles&quot; against Obfuscate, inasmuch as they seem perfectly balanced. If your Auspex is higher than someone's Obfuscate, you see through it automatically; if their Obfuscate is higher, you're fooled automatically. If they're even, you roll off, and only in the event of a tie does the defender (i.e., the obfuscate user) take the square. That's pretty even; the only way it could be more even would be if, instead of ties going to the defender, the players just had to keep rolling off until one person won--that would be a <i>de minimis</i> change; more for edge cases than anything else.<br /> <br /> I very strongly disagree your statement about Potence v. Fortitude though--i.e., that Potence beating out Fortitude isn't an intended feature. How could it be the case that someone designed the game with two powers that work <i>directly </i>against one another (one assisting damage rolls, and the other assisting soak rolls), but it not be an intentional shift in the power dynamics and tone of the game to make it so that the power that assists damage rolls is vastly and incomparably better than the power that assists soak rolls? Do you really believe that it was never brought to the designers' attention that an attacker with as much Potence as the defender has Fortitude, is incredibly favored? I will submit to you that even if when they wrote it all out that <i>wasn't </i>the intention, the moment it was pointed out to them, and they did nothing about it, they ratified the power imbalance as not-a-problem-here and it became their intent to make a game in which causing damage was incredibly easier than absorbing or preventing damage.<br /> <br /> Not only that, the fact alone that Celerity changed so much from one edition to the next (between how much blood you needed to spend for extra actions, all the way to V20 where your celerity buffs your Dex rolls when you're actively using them for extra turns), but that Potence has always been automatic successes, and Fortitude has always been dice, only further drives home the fact that despite the fact that they were willing to adjust how physical disciplines worked between editions--the fact that it's easier to cause damage than take it was always, at a minimum, perfectly acceptable. To their credit, they absolutely made a world that is Very Dark and Dangerous<b>\u2122.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages 20th actually has a far more balanced version of Potence/Fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:14:32-07:00","id":1384395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1384377#post1384377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Ages 20th actually has a far more balanced version of Potence/Fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's basically <i>perfectly</i> balanced -- but then, V20 Dark Ages does precisely the opposite of what I point out as being unbalanced above. They're both just dice, unless you spend a Blood Point, in which case they're both automatic successes. The only thing that put Potence <i>marginally</i> ahead Potence as an overall Discipline is that automatic Fortitude successes don't work against Fire and Sunlight (for obvious reasons--if fire and sunlight can only do 3 damage per turn, and you have Fort. 3, you would basically just become immune to the singular thing that vampires are supposed to be <i>most</i> vulnerable to). Then again, it's not like it's super likely one vampire will attack another in such a manner that they're attacking them with fireor sunlight (of all things), <i>and </i>get to apply their Potence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:18:26-07:00","id":1384397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1384376#post1384376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> did you even read the fucking thread?<br /> <br /> I LOVE THE TREMERE. <br /> <br /> that's why I made the flaw. so they'd be more unique. <br /> <br /> its not like I hate them, and I said that earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving them a 10 point flaw is a nice