"value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:14:45-07:00","id":1385712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1384811#post1384811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. Not sure why people would see this as someone hating on the Tremere though as it seems to add a lot of flavor which is what I like the most about it.<br /> <br /> I would agree with others though this game is far from balanced and I wouldn\u2019t worry to much about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks. I appreciate the support.<br /> and yes, this flaw is designed to add flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T23:56:32-07:00","id":1462977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1384836#post1384836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, think the Tremere are near perfect in V20. The thing with Tremere is that they're a really deep clan that on the surface looks really bad, so people get really upset at Tremere changes because &quot;If only you understood the Tremere like I do you wouldn't want to change them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>can you elaborate?<br /> <br /> im not sure what you mean here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T23:57:03-07:00","id":1462978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1376190#post1376190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Translation Guide had the great idea of making the Tremere a Covenant becuase they actually work like one...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>what are covenants???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T00:14:47-07:00","id":1462979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1376167#post1376167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3148_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3148\" data-vbnamecard=\"3148\">Zennis</a><br /> <br /> Oh, okay. I'm sorry I didn't realize that you meant they still had the clan flaw from V20, p69.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure why I took the following to mean that they &quot;possess no unique clan flaw&quot;... such as becoming bound after two drinks rather than three.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It was my mistake. I should have read more carefully. I may have been confused by this part of your post:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since your post was titled &quot;Alternate Clan Flaw&quot; I also thought you meant the loss of Auspex and Dominate was <i>instead</i> of the V20 flaw, rather than in addition to it.<br /> <br /> Again, sorry for misreading.</div> </div> </div> </div>you know I forgot to say that I really appreciate your humility here. man I wish some other people showed that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T06:11:46-07:00","id":1462995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1462978#post1462978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what are covenants???</div> </div> </div> </div>A covenant is basically the Requiem version of a Sect (Camarilla, Sabbat, Inconnu), but a bit more focused instead of an all-encompassing umbrella.<br /> <br /> I disagree that the Tremere make more sense as an organization rather than a clan, because it would undermine the shared history as a once mortal Hermetic House of mages and replace it with a generic association of vampire magicians.<br /> <br /> As a Clan, if they do not pick you as a mortal to be Embraced, your odds of earning the right to learn Thaumaturgy and their many paths and rituals from this is slim at best. It is an exclusive club with a limited window of entry after which getting in becomes virtually impossible (at best one might teach you a bit of their magic as a boon, but you\u2019ll never be a REAL member with unrestricted access).<br /> <br /> As an organization, a vampire can theoretically join at any time and be inducted into the society and eventually climb the ranks regardless of their initial status. It takes the exclusive club whose membership is based almost entirely on lineage and replaces it with a meritocracy.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a VERY different feeling and presentation; it makes it into something almost noble instead of the batch of exclusive assholes people only put up with because of their monopoly on magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T07:42:34-07:00","id":1462999,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a big Tremere fan and I think that this is a reasonable Clan flaw. In some ways it\u2019s fairly punishing, but as long as you allow Tremere to put their starting Discipline points into Disciplines other than Thaumaturgy, then it\u2019s not bad. In fact, it might allow greater flexibility if you let them put those points into any non-exclusive Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I do like them having Auspex and Dominate, they fit thematically with the Clan and, regarding origin, I could see the founders of the Clan starting out as mechanically Caitiff but over the vampiric generations, Auspex and Dominate were so often used and were the Disciplines most frequently passed from site to childe that those Disciplines became Clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also played in a number of games where I saw Tremere do cool stuff with Auspex and Dominate. The last Tremere I played was an economist who was embraced to help the Clan manage their money, he had no knowledge of magic and instead focused on Dominate and Auspex. In a LARP I was in, my wife played a Tremere and almost everything she did was based on Auspex. She stayed close to the Prince and used Auspex to sense emotions, read thoughts, and spot hidden spies, etc. It was actually a great relationship between a Ventrue Prince and Tremere, fitting into the themes of both Clans.<br /> <br /> So I like the 3 Disciplines that they have now, but I also think this is a nice flaw too. I honestly don\u2019t think that they need a Clan flaw in addition to their traditional one of being partially blood bound to their elders and generally being under the thumb of their elders. Of course, sometimes that isn\u2019t much of a flaw at all, sometimes it\u2019s the most crippling flaw. A lot of Clan flaws are like that, they all depend on the ST creating scenarios where the flaw comes into play but doesn\u2019t completely dominate the game.<br /> <br /> I think that the V5 flaw isn\u2019t bad, but it doesn\u2019t seem that thematic for me. I don\u2019t particularly like the flaw that lets them be blood bond with only two sips of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:50:23-07:00","id":1463015,"title":"","content":"What I make is that tremere face higher dificulties/penalities to all rolls against higher rank members including social ones.<br /> <br /> EDIT:They also face social disadvantages in rolls becuase people distrust them but that is a social mechanic, not their actual bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T17:52:22-07:00","id":1463036,"title":"","content":"My idea from v20 was Tremere have to pass a diff 6 courage roll to enter a persons house without invitation a with spike to 10 if they're explicitly denied entrance a fail denies them entrance for a night and a botch denies them entrance indenfinatly, entrance cannot be co-erced. This combines the concepts of conscent (Salubri) and territory (tzmisce).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T19:30:24-07:00","id":1463044,"title":"","content":"If I were going to give the Tremere a new flaw that was supernatural/physical in nature and not purely social, I think that I might actually divorce them from the Tzimisce and Salubri somewhat - that their ritual wasn\u2019t merely a fancy embrace with Tzimisce blood and that they lost some certain vampiric quality that other Clans have.<br /> <br /> No Clans Disciplines is one way to do this and I think it\u2019s a reasonable flaw, though I would miss Auspex and Dominate. <br /> <br /> Maybe difficulty embracing without a ritual. That could be an interesting and thematic flaw - the ritual is known to the Inner Circle and a few others, the Tremere cannot embrace without it. That might create too many repercussions about Anarch Tremere, but I think it\u2019s fitting. <br /> <br /> Another possibility is that Tremere blood has a certain thinness to it, maybe their blood pool is several points lower than it should be according to generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T20:02:39-07:00","id":1463046,"title":"","content":"Nagaraja are actually also a bloodline that stole their weakness from preexisting vampires.<br /> <br /> Still like concept of this idea though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:36:44-07:00","id":1463081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463044#post1463044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were going to give the Tremere a new flaw that was supernatural/physical in nature and not purely social, I think that I might actually divorce them from the Tzimisce and Salubri somewhat - that their ritual wasn\u2019t merely a fancy embrace with Tzimisce blood and that they lost some certain vampiric quality that other Clans have.<br /> <br /> No Clans Disciplines is one way to do this and I think it\u2019s a reasonable flaw, though I would miss Auspex and Dominate. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really true, crunchwise they're not actually particularly distinct from other clans. Fluff wise they're just a weird bloodline made good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T06:58:30-07:00","id":1463089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463081#post1463081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really true, crunchwise they're not actually particularly distinct from other clans. Fluff wise they're just a weird bloodline made good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is true mechanically that Tremere aren't different from other vampires. On the other hand, they aren't that mechanically similar to the Tzimisce or Salubri, aside from having Auspex. Though I think that it would be interesting to make the Tremere flaw based on losing some inherent vampiric quality because of becoming vampires through a magical ritual rather than the standard embrace. In some regards I get the impression that the Tremere founders could have just bled themselves to death and then be given vampire blood, though I think it would be thematically cool if the ritual had some more significant effect than the standard embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T09:10:04-07:00","id":1463105,"title":"","content":"One prospect if you\u2019re looking at the ritual as something that \u201cwashed\u201d the blood used of its Clan associations would be that they actually find the Animalism and Vicissitude disciplines more difficult or even impossible to learn and, as opposed to the Tzimisce bond with their native territory, the Tremere are instead \u201cunbound\u201d and have difficulty forming connections.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a penalty to social checks related to empathy or personal connections would also be in order\u2026 the dislike of others for the Tremere is literally wired into their blood because ritual to strip the blood of the Tzimisce\u2019s connection to the land makes the Tremere unable to connect through anything other than the raw power of disciplines and the blood bond.<br /> <br /> It would be the flip of most end scenarios from the old Gehenna book (where Tremere invariably becomes [Tzimisce]\u2019s butt-monkey), but it would also be just as fitting if the Tremere were just flat out immune to Vicissitude (unable to use it or be affected for good or ill) because of how they were created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T18:19:39-07:00","id":1463179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463046#post1463046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nagaraja are actually also a bloodline that stole their weakness from preexisting vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they didn't.<br /> <br /> They didn't actually stole anything from any clan, but instead their fluff is that their hunger for human meat is a consequence of their particular ritual and do not really include the blood. It is an interesting take that already calls to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a>'s idea for the Tremere, they follow the same rule mechanically but in lore aren't real Kindred in any sense, they're a Paradox-filled aberration with just some resonance to the immortal creatures the Euthanatoi comprehended most.<br /> <br /> By the way, their ritual was a simplified version of Isis' original <i>Spell of Life</i> that created the first mummies, and they received that spell directly from the Cult of Isis and adapted because they couldn't comprehend the full spell.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with Sergeant. The Circle of Seven were already capable Masters with centuries of life and advanced magic before the ritual, and they knew what a vampire is and what a simple Embrace would do to their Avatars. They were also expert alchemists. It is too contrived to say that a simple blood mix would alleviate their fears, they had reason to believe it was safe even if they got it wrong in the end.<br /> <br /> My favorite take is that they actually don't have the capacity to form the Blood Bond without a ritual, maybe a fairly advanced one. So lore-wise they have, instead of a weakness, precisely the lack of a vampiric ability. This could be extended to other powers of the Blood, like Ghouling and Embracing. You don't need to take away the 1-step weakness, although I would. Instead of this, merely keeping some of the neonate's blood for use against them seems enough to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T21:05:55-07:00","id":1463194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463179#post1463179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they didn't.<br /> <br /> They didn't actually stole anything from any clan, but instead their fluff is that their hunger for human meat is a consequence of their particular ritual and do not really include the blood. It is an interesting take that already calls to <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s idea for the Tremere, they follow the same rule mechanically but in lore aren't real Kindred in any sense, they're a Paradox-filled aberration with just some resonance to the immortal creatures the Euthanatoi comprehended most.<br /> <br /> By the way, their ritual was a simplified version of Isis' original <i>Spell of Life</i> that created the first mummies, and they received that spell directly from the Cult of Isis and adapted because they couldn't comprehend the full spell.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with Sergeant. The Circle of Seven were already capable Masters with centuries of life and advanced magic before the ritual, and they knew what a vampire is and what a simple Embrace would do to their Avatars. They were also expert alchemists. It is too contrived to say that a simple blood mix would alleviate their fears, they had reason to believe it was safe even if they got it wrong in the end.<br /> <br /> My favorite take is that they actually don't have the capacity to form the Blood Bond without a ritual, maybe a fairly advanced one. So lore-wise they have, instead of a weakness, precisely the lack of a vampiric ability. This could be extended to other powers of the Blood, like Ghouling and Embracing. You don't need to take away the 1-step weakness, although I would. Instead of this, merely keeping some of the neonate's blood for use against them seems enough to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry mistyped weakness when I meant vampirism. That said, the simplified spell was modified to use Setite blood, which made them vampires. Similar to the rituals Tremere used, although they primarily used Tzimisce blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T23:30:02-07:00","id":1463196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463194#post1463194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry mistyped weakness when I meant vampirism. That said, the simplified spell was modified to use Setite blood, which made them vampires. Similar to the rituals Tremere used, although they primarily used Tzimisce blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It stays as a fairly different process from the Embrace. They didn't contracted the Curse of Caine more than they replicated something similar through their magic. And in both cases the result is indeed something else, if not entirely. Neither the Nagaraja or the Tremere have actual clan witnesses in lore originally, the former suffer a defect from their own magic, the later from their own practices. Making the Tremere easier to bound to anyone was a later development to adjust their weakness for playability.<br /> <br /> And both must consider Mage lore to some degree when talking about their origins and themes, because both are born from Mage lore directly. The Nagaraja as the Chakravanti representatives in Wraith-Enoch, IIRC even with living sorcerers living there as their primary &quot;members&quot; and pool for Embraces. The Tremere predate the books of Mage but are a direct port from <i>Ars Magika</i>, literally source lore of the Order of Hermes and canonically the state of the Order before the war. They're both created fully with Mage in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T11:50:33-07:00","id":1463245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1463196#post1463196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It stays as a fairly different process from the Embrace. They didn't contracted the Curse of Caine more than they replicated something similar through their magic. And in both cases the result is indeed something else, if not entirely. Neither the Nagaraja or the Tremere have actual clan witnesses in lore originally, the former suffer a defect from their own magic, the later from their own practices. Making the Tremere easier to bound to anyone was a later development to adjust their weakness for playability.<br /> <br /> And both must consider Mage lore to some degree when talking about their origins and themes, because both are born from Mage lore directly. The Nagaraja as the Chakravanti representatives in Wraith-Enoch, IIRC even with living sorcerers living there as their primary &quot;members&quot; and pool for Embraces. The Tremere predate the books of Mage but are a direct port from <i>Ars Magika</i>, literally source lore of the Order of Hermes and canonically the state of the Order before the war. They're both created fully with Mage in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yes, but also no. Here's the thing, even if they're made with mage lore in mind, they aren't mages anymore. They're distinctly vampires in blood, it's clear in every way in modern lore. Regardless of magics that originally birthed the bloodlines, they are vampires now. At least modern lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:45:34-07:00","id":1463494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1375774-alternate-tremere-clan-flaw-no-in-clan-disciplines-v20?p=1462999#post1462999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a big Tremere fan and I think that this is a reasonable Clan flaw. In some ways it\u2019s fairly punishing, but as long as you allow Tremere to put their starting Discipline points into Disciplines other than Thaumaturgy, then it\u2019s not bad. In fact, it might allow greater flexibility if you let them put those points into any non-exclusive Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I do like them having Auspex and Dominate, they fit thematically with the Clan and, regarding origin, I could see the founders of the Clan starting out as mechanically Caitiff but over the vampiric generations, Auspex and Dominate were so often used and were the Disciplines most frequently passed from site to childe that those Disciplines became Clan Disciplines.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also played in a number of games where I saw Tremere do cool stuff with Auspex and Dominate. The last Tremere I played was an economist who was embraced to help the Clan manage their money, he had no knowledge of magic and instead focused on Dominate and Auspex. In a LARP I was in, my wife played a Tremere and almost everything she did was based on Auspex. She stayed close to the Prince and used Auspex to sense emotions, read thoughts, and spot hidden spies, etc. It was actually a great relationship between a Ventrue Prince and Tremere, fitting into the themes of both Clans.<br /> <br /> So I like the 3 Disciplines that they have now, but I also think this is a nice flaw too. I honestly don\u2019t think that they need a Clan flaw in addition to their traditional one of being partially blood bound to their elders and generally being under the thumb of their elders. Of course, sometimes that isn\u2019t much of a flaw at all, sometimes it\u2019s the most crippling flaw. A lot of Clan flaws are like that, they all depend on the ST creating scenarios where the flaw comes into play but doesn\u2019t completely dominate the game.<br /> <br /> I think that the V5 flaw isn\u2019t bad, but it doesn\u2019t seem that thematic for me. I don\u2019t particularly like the flaw that lets them be blood bond with only two sips of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take ion this is that they have created other paths to compensate. I often allow paths of sorcery from mage the ascension (NOT to be confused with spheres). <br /> <br /> Some of the paths are quite flexible and open ended as they allow for both ritual and fast casting as well as spending successes to tailor the effects you cause. <br /> <br /> I have no problem with the Termere developing paths of thaumaturgy which actually replicate the effect of other disciplines, provided they do so either at an inferior level or are more blood costly than the discipline in question typically is. Keeping in mind that it does require a point of blood to use any power of thaumaturgy whereas Auspex and dominate (as well as other disciplines) often do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T16:46:43-07:00","id":1463495,"title":"","content":"I for one made the divination and fascination paths of sorcery into thaumaturgy paths and modified them to function more like auspex and dominate. So the clan can still have its fancy psychic powers and mind control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","user":"Zennis","date":". 10-17-2021, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}